body:
## What

Makes the OpenChamber external-attach (openchamber#766) durable. Today it exists only as a hand-applied systemd drop-in on the laptop (`~/.config/systemd/user/openchamber.service.d/external-opencode.conf` with `OPENCODE_HOST` / `OPENCODE_SKIP_START` / `OPENCODE_PASSWORD`), which survives reboots but not a fresh provision. This PR expresses the same attach in the home-manager config.

## Changes

- **`bin/openchamber-start.sh`** (new, executable) — fleet-pattern start wrapper in the style of `bin/commandcode-proxy-start.sh`. It:
  - reads the standing OpenCode server's password at start time from `~/.local/state/opencode/service-prod.json` (`jq -r .password`) — runtime read only; the password is never written into the Nix store, a unit file, or this repo;
  - exports `OPENCODE_HOST` (default `http://127.0.0.1:13420`), `OPENCODE_SKIP_START=true`, and `OPENCODE_PASSWORD`;
  - fails loudly (exit 1, clear stderr message) if the state file is missing/unreadable or has no password, rather than letting OpenChamber spawn a managed instance;
  - execs the real serve script passed as its argument.
- **`home/common/default.nix`**:
  - new `openchamberUnitStart` shim (`writeShellScript "openchamber-start-unit"`) that execs `bash "$HOME/code/bin/openchamber-start.sh"` with the existing `openchamberStart` serve script as its argument — the same checkout-wrapper pattern as `commandcode-proxy`;
  - the `openchamber` unit's `ExecStart` now points at the shim. Everything else is unchan
